    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Bryson Stott** (72.46) and **Tyler Freeman** (68.35) headline our offensive output. **Bryson Stott** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against V\u00e1squez, as the SP skill adjustment (+18%) and his platoon advantage drive his value well into the \"Strong\" category. Similarly, **Tyler Freeman** is a high-upside play; despite the lineup being pending, his projected #2 slot against the hittable Rodriguez, G provides the perfect environment for a high-volume performance. **Daulton Varsho** (62.08) also earns a start, with the algorithm specifically noting the slow delivery of Elder, which should create prime opportunities for **Daulton Varsho** to capitalize on his elite sprint speed and boost our stolen base count.\n\nNavigating the bench required a disciplined approach to our efficiency floor. **Masyn Winn** (37.52) was the most difficult exclusion, ultimately failing to clear the 40-point threshold due to a difficult matchup against Eovaldi and an unfavorable wind condition that penalized his raw projection. We are also monitoring the status of **Cal Raleigh**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while **Will Smith** and **Lawrence Butler** sit due to scheduled rest. We continue to prioritize our active roster depth, relying on the platoon advantages of **Gleyber Torres** (+13% vs. Matz) and **Taylor Ward** (+9% vs. Early) to drive production, even as **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Luis Arraez** face tighter matchups against tougher arms like Schlittler and Harrison, respectively. Managers should monitor the official lineup card for **Tyler Freeman**, as any shift out of the #2 hole would necessitate a re-evaluation of his current efficiency score.",
